---
description: Repository governance — shared agent instructions and blueprint rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. It is the single source of instructions for all agents and humans in this repo.

Short version:
- Read `blueprint/00-product-core.md` and the blueprint documents relevant to the task before changing code.
- Never edit `blueprint/00-product-core.md`. Propose changes to `approved` blueprint files; don't make them silently.
- Fill in the Blueprint impact table in every PR (`none | updated | proposed | deviation` per document 00–07).
- Reference acceptance criteria IDs (`AC-nnn.n`) in tests. Record intentional differences as a deviation (`npx product-blueprint@0.3.0 new deviation "<title>"`).
- Never weaken lint rules, tests or CI checks to get a green build.
- Blueprint still empty templates in a repo with code? Setting it up means following the onboarding spec: `npx product-blueprint@0.3.0 docs WF-00`.
